# UITK Lock — All Created UI

**Any UI you create is UI Toolkit only.** No new uGUI (`Canvas`, `Image`, `TextMeshProUGUI`, `MenuUiBuilder`).

How to build it: `dark-matter-genesis-ui-toolkit.mdc`.

## Do

- Layout: `Assets/UI Toolkit/Screens/<Screen>.uxml`
- Styles: screen `.uss` + `DarkMatterGenesis.uss`
- Runtime: `Assets/UI Toolkit/Runtime/DMUiToolkit*.cs` on an existing `UIDocument` host
- Colors: `DarkMatterGenesisUiPalette` / Shift theme
- Bind with `root.Q<T>("name")`. Hide unused hosts in C# only (never USS `display: none` in Builder files).

## Do not

- Add a second HUD `UIDocument` / Panel Settings
- Ship a uGUI fallback “just in case”
- Expand leftover MainCanvas / Invector uGUI when touching a surface — extend UITK instead

## Hot Cross icons

Gameplay crossbar (`HotCross.uxml` / `DMUiToolkitHotCross`) uses **only** the alpha cutouts in:

`Assets/_Project/Art/UI/HotCrossIcons`

Do not put plated `ItemData.icon` / `Art/Icons` tiles on the Hot Cross. Inventory may keep those tiles.

## Exception

uGUI only if the user **explicitly** asks for that surface, or the target is third-party UI that cannot be UITK-wrapped yet.
